on, sets its default to 'y'.  Since we do not actually have any STM SoC supported by chromeos-4.12, let's turn it back off via config.  echo &quot;# CONFIG_DRM_STM is not set&quot; &gt;&gt; chromeos/config/armel/common.config ./chromeos/scripts/kernelconfig oldconfig  Accept all defaults.  Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=b:66735140 TEST=Normalize configs,   Ensure &quot;CONFIG_FB_PROVIDE_GET_FB_UNMAPPED_AREA is not set&quot; in base.config  Change-Id: Ie5c176617e1d43b37fc51ad2818563ac879c4cb0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/706252 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="706252" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/52/706252/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iad2743da7f671508b6ad6e026928df838de72cb2" commit="637995b2b6cc4175f22abac63cd4e4a141e0181d" commit_message="UI USE flags: add optional ARC UI scaling factor  VMs can force the scaling factor of Android apps since detection of the monitor will return potentially incorrect results. Add &quot;arc_force_2x_scaling&quot; USE flag for to force the scaling factor to 2x.  BUG=b:66963637 TEST=run novato image, check dimensions of Android app windows  Change-Id: Iad2743da7f671508b6ad6e026928df838de72cb2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/690617 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Norvez &lt;norvez@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Norvez &lt;norvez@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mitsuru Oshima &lt;oshima@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="690617" owner_email="norvez@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://c